                        "text": "How much credit deposit can 'Balaka Bank Ltd.' create? Explain.",
                        "answer": "According to the stem, Balaka Bank Ltd. can create a total credit deposit of BDT 40,000,000 (40 Lakhs) from the primary deposit.\n\n\nCredit creation through deposits refers to the process where commercial banks multiply their initial primary deposits into multiple derivative deposits through consecutive lending. When a customer deposits cash, it is a primary deposit. The bank maintains a certain percentage of this deposit as a statutory cash reserve (Required Reserve Ratio or $RRR$) and lends out the excess reserves. This loan amount is not paid in cash but credited to a new account, creating a derivative deposit. The formula for total credit deposit creation is:\n\n$$\\text{Total Credit Deposit} = \\frac{\\text{Primary Deposit}}{\\text{Reserve Ratio}}$$\n\n\n\nIn the given stem, Mr. Mohsin made a primary deposit of BDT 10,000,000 (10 Lakhs) in Balaka Bank Ltd., and the bank maintains a 20% reserve ratio ($0.20$). Substituting these values into the formula:\n\n$$\\text{Total Credit Deposit} = \\frac{1,000,000}{0.20} = 5,000,000 \\text{ BDT}$$\n\n\nSince the question asks for the amount of credit deposit created (derivative deposits generated), we subtract the initial primary deposit from the total deposit:\n\n$$\\text{Derivative Credit Deposit Created} = 5,000,000 - 1,000,000 = 4,000,000 \\text{ BDT}$$\n\n\nTherefore, Balaka Bank Ltd. can create an additional BDT 40 Lakhs in credit deposits."
