                "answer": "\"For the dignity of a cheque, it should be prepared correctly\" means that a cheque must strictly adhere to all legal and formal technical requirements to be honored (maintained in high structural standing) by a bank. If a cheque contains structural flaws—such as mismatched amounts in words and figures, a missing drawer's signature, date alterations without counter-signatures, or an expired date—the bank is legally forced to dishonor it.Dishonoring a cheque damages the commercial reputation, trust, and creditworthiness of the drawer in the business marketplace. Therefore, to ensure that the payment instrument executes smoothly and the drawer avoids potential legal liabilities or loss of institutional prestige, every element of the cheque leaf must be meticulously and flawlessly written."
