                        "text": "What is meant by the restrictive endorsement of a cheque?",
                        "answer": "A restrictive endorsement (সীমিত বা সীমাবদ্ধ অনুমোদন) refers to an act of signing on the back of an order cheque where the holder restricts or completely blocks any further transfer of its ownership to someone else.By using specific phrases like \"Pay to X only\" (শুধু এক্সকে প্রদান করুন), the endorser eliminates the negotiable character of the instrument, legally binding the bank to disburse the funds strictly to the named individual and preventing further circulating endorsements."
