                "category": "Comprehension",
                "question": "What is meant by bank funds?",
                "answer": "Bank funds refer to the total aggregate capital that a commercial bank mobilizes from internal and external sources to run its operations, maintain statutory liquidity, and advance loans to borrowers.\n\n\nA bank's funds are composed of its primary capital (paid-up capital, statutory reserves, retained earnings) and its secondary borrowed capital (customer deposits, central bank loans, inter-bank call money). Managing this pool effectively is the core operational objective of banking institutions. The bank transforms these liability-side funds into asset-side wealth by deploying them into profitable avenues like commercial loans, treasury bills, and government securities, earning an interest spread that serves as the bank's primary revenue stream."
