                "answer": "The primary and most essential source of funds for a commercial bank is customer deposits (আমানত).\n\n\nCommercial banks function primarily as financial intermediaries that mobilize idle savings from surplus units (the public) and channel them to deficit units (borrowers). These deposits come in various forms, such as current, savings, and fixed deposit accounts. Since internal capital (like paid-up capital and reserves) is limited, customer deposits form the massive bulk of the bank's operational loanable fund. The bank uses this low-cost mobilized capital to advance loans at a higher interest rate, earning a profit margin from the interest rate differential (spread)."
