                "category": "Comprehension",
                "question": "Why is the customer's character a crucial consideration in sanctioning a loan? Explain.",
                "answer": "The customer's character is a crucial consideration because it reflects their honesty, integrity, and genuine willingness to honor financial obligations, which serves as the ultimate moral guarantee for loan recovery.\n\n\nIn credit management, a borrower's financial capacity or collateral means very little if they lack the intent to repay. An individual with strong personal and professional character will make every possible effort to clear their liabilities, even during business losses or economic downturns. Conversely, a borrower with weak character may intentionally default or divert funds despite having the capacity to pay. Therefore, assessing character helps banks minimize credit risks, prevent willful defaults, and maintain the structural safety of their loan portfolio."
