                "answer": "Determining the exchange rate is crucial in import-export trade because it directly establishes the relative value of domestic currency against foreign currencies, which determines the actual cost of imports and the profitability of exports.\n\n\nIn international commerce, global currencies continuously fluctuate based on market forces. If the exchange rate is not clearly defined, global merchants cannot calculate their profit margins, price their commodities, or estimate their total tax liabilities. A stable and predictable exchange rate layout minimizes the currency risk for businesses, protects international merchants from sudden monetary losses, and allows central banks to manage foreign reserves efficiently, serving as the baseline infrastructure for global commercial stability."
