                        "answer": "Mr. Azad secured his subsequent expansion loan of BDT 30 lakh based on a combination of 'Impersonal/Material Security' (বস্তুগত জামানত) and 'Personal Security' (ব্যক্তিগত জামানত).\n\n\n1. Impersonal/Material Security (Mortgage of the Farm): To secure the larger BDT 30 lakh development loan, Mr. Azad placed his entire physical poultry farm under a formal mortgage with Madhumati Bank. A mortgage is a legal charge established over immovable fixed assets, such as land and commercial buildings, where the deeds are held by the lender as an ultimate safety cushion. If the poultry business faces insolvency or defaults on its debt servicing, the bank holds the statutory authority to auction the physical real estate and infrastructure to recover its principal and accrued compound interest fully.\n\n\n2. Personal Security (Third-Party Recommendation/Guarantee): In addition to the material land mortgage, Mr. Azad backed the credit line using a recommendation from a prominent, reputable individual (বিশিষ্ট ব্যক্তির সুপারিশ). In banking jurisprudence, when a high-net-worth individual or a respected market figure formally recommends or signs off on a borrower's credit line, it functions as a personal security or guarantor credit enhancement. The bank values this moral asset because the guarantor's social standing and financial capacity serve as a secondary assurance of repayment, bridging the trust gap for large capital outlays.\n\n\nIn conclusion, Madhumati Bank utilized a balanced, dual-layered risk mitigation strategy to underwrite Mr. Azad's expansion project. By anchoring the BDT 30 lakh loan with a solid, appreciating immovable property (the farm structures) and reinforcing it with high-reputation personal backing, the bank successfully satisfied the safety and security principles of lending. This comprehensive structural approach protected public deposit funds while providing the poultry enterprise with the vital capital required to expand its agricultural production capacity."
