                        "text": "How rational do you think the foreign exchange rate determination method indicated in the stem is? Explain with arguments.",
                        "answer": "The method of exchange rate determination indicated in the stem is the 'Demand and Supply Theory' (Floating Exchange Rate System), and it is highly rational and superior because it automatically aligns currency values with real economic health.\n\n\n1. Automatic Market Equilibrium through Trade Flows: The stem notes that the value of the Dollar dropped during the transaction cycle because of shifting macro conditions. Under a market-driven Floating Exchange Rate System, currency pricing is not artificially manipulated by state regimes; instead, it responds dynamically to international trade volumes, capital inflows, and market liquidity. When national imports drop or foreign inflows rise, the local demand for the Dollar falls, causing the domestic currency to strengthen organically. This automatic adjustment mechanism serves as an excellent economic stabilizer for the broader financial ecosystem.\n\n\n2. Superiority Over Rigid Macro-Theoretical Pricing Models: The primary alternative framework—the Purchasing Power Parity (PPP) theory—attempts to lock currency values based on a static basket of cross-border goods. While theoretically elegant for long-term academic tracking, PPP is highly impractical for daily international commerce because it completely ignores immediate transaction liquidities, transport overheads, tariffs, and speculative capital flights. Employing a floating supply-and-demand framework ensures that merchants are trading under highly transparent, accurate, and instantly responsive real-world pricing structures.\n\n\n3. Prevention of Black Markets and Capital Flight: When central banks try to artificially fix exchange rates against market realities, it leads to rapid foreign reserve exhaustion and fuels illegal hundi channels. A flexible, market-determined system eliminates this structural risk. While exchange rate volatility can occasionally create minor financial hurdles for individual exporters like Mr. Kamal when the dollar dips prior to bill liquidation, it forces businesses to adopt modern financial risk-management tools like forward hedging contracts to secure their target margins.\n\n\nIn conclusion, the demand-and-supply driven exchange rate framework remains the most rational and efficient method for modern global trade. It acts as an automated economic thermostat that continuously re-balances international accounts without causing structural distortions. By letting open market forces dictate rates, the financial ecosystem maintains high operational transparency, protects national reserves from artificial depletion, and creates a highly resilient environment for long-term cross-border trade execution."
