                        "answer": "Determining the exchange rate is critically important in import-export trade because it directly dictates the financial profitability, pricing competitiveness, and real-world cash-flow calculations of global merchants.\n\n\nIn international commerce, transactions are conducted using different sovereign currencies, meaning an exporter's local earnings and an importer's local expenditures depend entirely on the conversion rate. For an exporter, an increase in the value of foreign currency (like the US Dollar) against the local currency expands their net profit margins in domestic cash terms without requiring any production increase. Conversely, for an importer, exchange rate volatility can cause rapid inflation in raw material costs, rendering their business model unsustainable. Therefore, an accurate and predictable exchange rate framework is indispensable for managing financial risk, establishing stable product pricing, and facilitating international trade security."
