                "category": "Comprehension",
                "question": "Why is a mortality table important in life insurance?",
                "answer": "A mortality table (মৃত্যুহারপঞ্জি) is highly critical in life insurance because it provides the scientific and statistical baseline needed to calculate premium rates accurately.By charting the historical probability of death for individuals at various ages, it allows actuaries to forecast future claim frequencies and calculate average life expectancies. Without this data, life insurance companies would be unable to assess risk profiles properly, leaving them vulnerable to setting premium rates too low to cover actual future payouts, which would threaten institutional solvency."
