                        "answer": "The insurance policy taken out by the owner of Jishan Garments on behalf of the workers is a \"Group Insurance Policy\" (গোষ্ঠী বিমাপত্র).According to insurance principles, a group insurance policy is a single master contract executed by an employer or organization to collectively cover the risk, health, or lives of a large body of individuals (typically employees) under one unified umbrella framework at a reduced premium cost.In the given stem, the management of Jishan Garments accepted the workers' demands and took out an insurance policy for all working workers collectively (কর্মরত সকল শ্রমিকদের কল্যাণের জন্য একটি বিমাপত্র). Instead of executing individual insurance policies for hundreds of workers separately, the owner brought the entire workforce under a single contract. This streamlined approach provides industrial social security, making it a classic example of a group insurance policy."
