                        "label": "d",
                        "text": "How much compensation can the workers affected by the accident receive? Give your opinion.",
                        "answer": "1. Evaluation of Compensation Framework:\n\nThe affected workers (the nominees of the deceased worker and the seven injured workers) will receive financial benefits strictly according to the pre-scheduled terms, limits, and sum assured specified in the master group insurance contract. However, in life and accident insurance, this payout is defined as a fixed contract benefit rather than a strict property indemnity settlement.2. Payout for the Deceased Worker:\n\nFor the single worker who unfortunately passed away in the factory accident, the insurance company is contractually obligated to disburse the full sum assured (বিমাঙ্ক) designated per capita under the group policy terms. This fixed lump-sum amount will be handed over to the legal heirs or registered nominees of the deceased worker to secure their family's immediate financial survival.3. Payout for the Injured Workers:\n\nFor the seven injured workers, the compensation amount will depend on the \"Group Accident and Disability\" clauses embedded in the policy leaf. The insurance company will not pay the full life sum assured to them; instead, they will disburse a mathematically calculated percentage of the coverage based on the severity of their physical injuries (e.g., temporary disability, permanent partial disability, or medical hospitalization costs) as certified by an approved medical board.4. Conclusion:\n\nIn conclusion, the affected workers cannot claim arbitrary or infinite compensation from the insurer; their financial recovery is strictly capped by the maximum limits set in Jishan Garments' master policy. The owner's prompt submission of the claim ensures that the insurance provider will swiftly process and distribute these vital safety funds, mitigating the economic distress caused by the workplace disaster."
