                "answer": "Concept: Jettison (পণ্য নিক্ষেপণ) results in a \"General Average Loss\" (সাধারণ গড় ক্ষতি) under maritime and insurance regulations.\n\n\nExplanation: A general average loss occurs when a portion of the cargo or ship equipment is intentionally and voluntarily sacrificed in an extreme emergency to protect the entire venture (the ship, the remaining cargo, and the crew) from total destruction. Since the sacrifice is made for the common safety of all stakeholders, the financial burden of this partial loss is shared proportionally by all parties who benefited from the rescue, rather than falling solely on the owner of the destroyed goods."
