                        "label": "b",
                        "text": "What kind of condition in a marine insurance contract is the legality of the insured property? Explain.",
                        "answer": "Concept: The legality of the insured property is an \"Implied Warranty\" (অব্যক্ত শর্ত) in a marine insurance contract.\n\n\nExplanation: Implied warranties are fundamental conditions that are not explicitly written down in the policy document but are universally accepted by law and taken for granted. The legality of the adventure implies that the ship, its cargo, and the purpose of the voyage must comply entirely with national and international laws; any involvement in illegal trade or smuggling automatically invalidates the policy."
