                        "answer": "Concept: Constructive total loss (উদ্ধারযোগ্য সামগ্রিক ক্ষতি) occurs when the insured subject matter is heavily damaged or abandoned because its actual total loss appears unavoidable, or because the cost of repairing and recovering it would exceed its final restored value.\n\n\nExplanation: In this situation, the property (like a ship) is not completely destroyed or vanished, but it is practically useless from a financial standpoint. For example, if a ship gets stuck in a remote area and it costs 15 lakh Taka to salvage and repair it, but the ship's actual value is only 10 lakh Taka, the owner will legally abandon it to the insurer and claim full compensation for a total loss."
