                "question": "Why is moral hazard given special importance in fire insurance? Explain.",
                "answer": "Concept: Moral hazard (নৈতিক ঝুঁকি) refers to the risk that the insured might behave dishonestly or recklessly because they are protected by insurance.\n\n\nExplanation: Fire insurance is especially susceptible to moral hazard because, unlike natural disasters, a fire can easily be caused intentionally or facilitated by the negligence of the owner. If the insured has a motive (e.g., financial distress or over-insurance), they might orchestrate a fire to collect the insurance payout. Therefore, insurers prioritize assessing the character and intent of the insured to ensure they have no financial incentive to let their property burn down."
