                        "label": "d",
                        "text": "In light of the insurance system, provide your opinion on the future course of action the transport company should take to ensure compensation for office employees.",
                        "answer": "Inference/Claim: The company must shift from ad-hoc ex-gratia payments to systematic \"Group Life Insurance\" (দলগত জীবন বিমা) or \"Group Personal Accident Insurance\" (দলগত দুর্ঘটনা বিমা).\n\n\nTheoretic Rule (Systematic Risk Transfer): Ad-hoc payments (like the 10 lakh Taka) place an immense, unpredictable financial burden on the company. Insurance moves this burden to an insurer, providing guaranteed and consistent compensation to employees' families without straining the company’s capital reserves.\n\n\nScenario Analysis: The fire in the office occurred, but the fire insurance policy did not cover life. To prevent future financial and legal crises, the company should:\n\n1. Implement a Group Insurance Policy: This provides life and accident coverage for all office staff under a single policy, which is cost-effective.\n\n2. Worker's Compensation Insurance: Ensuring coverage specifically for industrial/workplace accidents.\n\n\nConclusion: By integrating these into their risk management strategy, the company transforms an unpredictable \"disaster expense\" into a predictable \"annual operational cost.\" This secures employee welfare, improves corporate reputation, and protects the company's financial future."
