                "explanation": "<p>A joint-stock company is an artificial legal entity. It raises funds via share distribution (i), has a legal personality to transact in its own name (ii), and possesses perpetual succession, meaning it can only be wound up via strict statutory legal procedures (iii). All are correct.</p>"
