                "explanation": "<p>1. If $\\frac{3}{4} \\times \\text{Total Salary} = 90,000\\text{ TK}$, then $\\text{Total Salary} = 90,000 \\times \\frac{4}{3} = 1,20,000\\text{ TK}$.<br><br>2. Outstanding portion is the remaining $\\frac{1}{4}$ share:<br><br>$\\text{Outstanding Salary} = 1,20,000 - 90,000 = 30,000\\text{ TK}$. (Note: Based on standard tracking grids, if the option choice lists 30,000 as B, it represents total outstanding. The remaining fraction $\\frac{1}{4}$ of total 1,20,000 yields 30,000 TK, matching Option B).</p>"
