            {
                "id": 8843,
                "text": "<p>Read the following stem and answer the question:</p><p>The inventory transactions of Lamia Traders for December 2020 are as follows:</p><p>Dec 1: Opening Stock 2,500 units @ 20 TK per unit.</p><p>Dec 13: Purchased 1,500 units @ 22 TK per unit.</p><p>Dec 21: Issued 2,800 units.</p><p>Dec 31: Purchased 1,200 units @ 18 TK per unit.</p><p>Q. What is the total value of the closing inventory at the end of the month under the FIFO method?</p>",
                "meta": "Viqarunnisa Noon School & College · 2025",
                "type": "college",
                "options": [
                    "21,600 TK",
                    "26,400 TK",
                    "45,600 TK",
                    "48,000 TK"
                ],
                "correctAnswer": 3,
                "explanation": "<p>1. Total stock units available before issue = $2,500 + 1,500 = 4,000$ units.<br><br>2. Dec 21 Issue: 2,800 units are issued. Under FIFO, they come from the oldest stock:<br><br>- All 2,500 units from Dec 1 batch (@ 20 TK).<br><br>- Remaining 300 units ($2,800 - 2,500$) from Dec 13 batch (@ 22 TK).<br><br>3. Remaining balance after issue: 1,200 units from the Dec 13 purchase batch (@ 22 TK) = 26,400 TK.<br><br>4. Dec 31 Purchase: New 1,200 units @ 18 TK = 21,600 TK are added.<br><br>5. $\\text{Total Value of Closing Inventory} = 26,400 + 21,600 = 48,000\\text{ TK}$.</p>"
            },
            {
                "id": 8844,
                "text": "<p>Read the following stem and answer the question:</p><p>The inventory transactions of Lamia Traders for December 2020 are as follows:</p><p>Dec 1: Opening Stock 2,500 units @ 20 TK per unit.</p><p>Dec 13: Purchased 1,500 units @ 22 TK per unit.</p><p>Dec 21: Issued 2,800 units.</p><p>Dec 31: Purchased 1,200 units @ 18 TK per unit.</p><p>Q. What is the per-unit price of the inventory issued on December 21 under the Weighted Average Method?</p>",
                "meta": "Viqarunnisa Noon School & College · 2025",
                "type": "college",
                "options": [
                    "20.00 TK",
                    "20.75 TK",
                    "21.00 TK",
                    "22.00 TK"
                ],
                "correctAnswer": 1,
                "explanation": "<p>1. To find the weighted average rate before the Dec 21 issue, calculate total units and total cost available up to that date (Dec 1 and Dec 13 batches).<br><br>2. Total Units available = $2,500 + 1,500 = 4,000$ units.<br><br>3. Total Cost available = $(2,500 \\times 20) + (1,500 \\times 22) = 50,000 + 33,000 = 83,000\\text{ TK}$.<br><br>4. $\\text{Weighted Average Rate per unit} = \\frac{\\text{Total Cost}}{\\text{Total Units}} = \\frac{83,000}{4,000} = 20.75\\text{ TK}$.<br><br>Therefore, the issue price on Dec 21 is 20.75 TK per unit.</p>"
            }
