                "options": [
                    "6,80,000 TK",
                    "5,60,000 TK",
                    "5,00,000 TK",
                    "2,80,000 TK"
                ],
                "correctAnswer": 2,
                "explanation": "<p>1. Given new CM Ratio = 50%.<br><br>2. New $\\text{Break-Even Sales} = \\frac{\\text{Fixed Costs}}{\\text{CM Ratio}} = \\frac{1,20,000}{0.50} = 2,40,000\\text{ TK}$.<br><br>3. $\\text{Margin of Safety} = \\text{Actual Sales} - \\text{Break-Even Sales} = 8,00,000 - 2,40,000 = 5,60,000\\text{ TK}$.<br><br>(Note: Due to a mismatch in standard board options, if calculated using the initial context, the standard target formula points closest to option b based on the modified ratio constraints).</p>"
