                        "answer": "Management cycle refers to the continuous and sequential process of performing core managerial functions—planning, organizing, staffing, directing, motivating, coordinating, and controlling—to achieve organizational goals.<br><br>It is called a cycle because it represents a recurring, never-ending process where the final stage (controlling) provides the baseline data, deviations, and feedback required to formulate the next new plan, starting the loop all over again."
