                        "answer": "By introducing new stoppages to adapt to market demand, Mr. 'K' follows the management principle of Flexibility.<br><br>The principle of flexibility dictates that management policies, strategies, and plans should not be rigid; rather, they must be dynamic and capable of changing or adjusting in response to shifting real-world situations, customer behaviors, or environmental factors.<br><br>According to the stem, Mr. 'K' initially started a rigid \"non-stop\" service, which resulted in financial losses as one-third of the seats remained empty. Recognizing the problem, he flexibly altered his original strategy by adding strategic stoppages in Chittagong and Comilla. This timely adjustment filled the empty seats and converted a failing venture into a profitable business, illustrating the perfect execution of flexibility."
