                        "answer": "Mr. Sohel is a mid-level (or middle-level) management officer.<br><br>Middle-level management acts as a bridge between top management and lower-level operational management, focusing on executing the broad plans, rules, and policies transmitted from the top by converting them into operational targets and supervising frontline supervisors.<br><br>According to the stem, Mr. Sohel receives direct orders from the Managing Director (top management) and translates those orders into operational guidelines for the department's supervisors (lower management). Since his structural role involves department-wide execution, target setting, and coordinating between top executives and floor supervisors, he explicitly belongs to mid-level management."
