                        "answer": "The management principle of Division of Work (along with the Principle of Order) is clearly reflected in the first phase of the stem.<br><br>The principle of division of work states that the entire workload of an enterprise should be divided into specialized tasks and assigned to individuals based on their specific skills and qualifications, while the principle of order dictates a systematic place for every material resource and human asset.<br><br>According to the stem, Rajan notices that his company systematically values individual merit and assigns specific tasks only to those workers who possess the corresponding operational skills. Furthermore, physical resources like production machines, dustbins, and safety walkways are placed efficiently in their scientifically designated positions, proving that management combines division of labor with strict material order to optimize efficiency."
