                        "label": "d",
                        "text": "Analyze what needs to be done to eliminate the dissatisfaction among the employees.",
                        "answer": "Elimination of Favoritism: To eliminate the deep-rooted dissatisfaction among the employees, the organization must strictly implement the \"Principle of Equity\" and ensure a transparent, merit-based promotion system, thereby curbing the regional bias practiced by the MD, Mr. Ashik.<br><br>The core issue of dissatisfaction stems from nepotism and regional favoritism. When an executive promotes individuals based on geographical origin rather than qualifications or performance, it shatters organizational justice. Employees lose motivation, loyalty declines, and internal conflicts arise because they feel their hard work will never be recognized over personal biases.<br><br>To resolve this crisis, the following measures should be analyzed and implemented immediately:<br><br>* Establish an Objective Performance Appraisal System: Promotions must be linked to quantified Key Performance Indicators (KPIs) rather than subjective managerial preferences.<br><br>* Formation of a Neutral Promotion Committee: Decision-making power regarding promotions should not rest solely with the MD; a diverse panel should review candidates to ensure neutrality.<br><br>* Strict Enforcement of Organizational Justice: The Chairman, Mr. Shafi, must intervene to enforce policies that prohibit any form of discrimination or regional favoritism within the corporate structure.<br><br>In conclusion, removing employee discontent requires transitioning from a person-centric bias to a rule-centric culture. By holding Mr. Ashik accountable and institutionalizing absolute fairness, the organization can restore faith, boost employee morale, and ensure sustainable productivity for Multi Investment Project (MIP)."
