                        "text": "What type of plan, on the basis of nature, is the plan in the stem? Explain.",
                        "answer": "The plan formulated by Mr. Kajal in the stem is a Standing plan (স্থায়ী পরিকল্পনা) in terms of its nature.<br><br>In management, a standing plan is a continuous, permanent guide designed to manage recurring and routine operations of an organization over an extended period. Once established, it remains operational for day-to-day production runs until long-term economic shifts make it obsolete.<br><br>In the stem, Mr. Kajal established an industrial cement manufacturing company meant for continuous production and operational stability. He mapped out a standard operational plan to run his factory's daily activities routinely from the beginning. Since this plan was designed to govern continuous, ongoing business operations rather than a single event, it is classified as a standing plan."
