                "questions": [
                    {
                        "label": "a",
                        "text": "What is an informal organization?",
                        "answer": "An informal organization is a structure that develops spontaneously within a formal organization based on personal relationships, shared interests, habits, or social interactions among employees, rather than official rules."
                    },
                    {
                        "label": "b",
                        "text": "Why is formal organization important for maintaining discipline? Explain.",
                        "answer": "Definition: Formal organization is highly important for maintaining discipline because it clearly defines the systematic rules, regulations, official lines of authority, and behavioral boundaries for everyone in the enterprise.<br><br>Explanation: Within a formal structure, every employee knows exactly who they report to, what their specific jurisdiction is, and the consequences of violating operational rules. This predetermined chain of command minimizes arbitrary behavior, eliminates guesswork, and creates institutional accountability, which prevents chaos and ensures a highly disciplined work environment."
                    },
                    {
                        "label": "c",
                        "text": "Which type of organizational structure is present in Scenario-2? Explain.",
                        "answer": "Identification: The organizational structure present in Scenario-2 is a Line Organizational Structure (also known as a Military Organization).<br><br>Definition & Linkage: A Line organizational structure is a framework where administrative authority flows vertically downward in a straight line from top executives to subordinates, and accountability moves directly upward. In Scenario-2, three branch heads work under a General Manager and are explicitly accountable directly to that General Manager for their activities, while subordinates strictly follow the orders of their respective branch heads.<br><br>Analysis: This setup establishes a clear, uncompromised scalar chain from top to bottom without any side-channel advisory committees or complex structural divisions. Since the flow of command and vertical accountability is direct, absolute, and unified, it perfectly reflects the fundamental characteristics of a Line organizational structure."
                    },
                    {
                        "label": "d",
                        "text": "Between Scenario-1 and Scenario-2, which one is suitable for specialization? Show your arguments by mentioning the type of organizational structure.",
                        "answer": "Argument & Type Selection: Between the two, Scenario-1 is highly suitable for specialization because its underlying framework is a Functional Organizational Structure, whereas Scenario-2 represents a Line organizational structure where specialization is absent.<br><br>Definition & Core Concept: A functional organizational structure divides an enterprise based on distinct nature of work or functions (such as purchase, marketing, production), placing a specialized expert at the head of each department. In Scenario-1, Chayan Industries explicitly breaks down its operations into specialized divisions (Purchase, Marketing, Production) and appoints qualified, work-experienced heads (Mr. X, Mr. Y, Mr. Z) to run them.<br><br>Comparative Evaluation: In Scenario-1, because work is divided according to specialization and managed by domain experts, employees can focus purely on mastering specific tasks, which significantly elevates operational efficiency, skill division, and professional growth. On the other hand, Scenario-2 relies on a Line structure where generalist branch managers must oversee all types of diverse work within their branch, leading to a lack of specialized supervision and an excessive workload.<br><br>Conclusion: Therefore, due to the explicit departmentalization based on specialized professional qualifications and functions, the structure in Scenario-1 (Functional Organization) is vastly superior and uniquely suited for achieving organizational specialization."
                    }
                ]
