                        "answer": "Definition: Promotion is given to elevate an efficient employee to a higher position of responsibility, status, and salary within the organization's hierarchy.<br><br>Explanation: It serves as a vital tool for employee motivation, recognition of merit, and boosting morale. By promoting competent internal candidates, an organization builds long-term institutional loyalty, retains highly skilled talent, reduces employee turnover, and ensures a continuous flow of experienced leadership across higher executive ranks."
