                        "answer": "Core Reason & Identification: Megha Automobile Ltd. was able to achieve its goal primarily due to the effectiveness of Employee Training and Development following a proper staffing process.<br><br>Definition & Context: Training is the formal process of enhancing an employee's professional knowledge, operational skills, and functional behavior to match the specific demands of a job. The stem explicitly notes that although there was a baseline coordination delay among the newly hired BUET engineers initially, the enterprise eventually fulfilled its strategic target successfully.<br><br>Evaluation of the Process: When raw, highly educated talent is hired via external campus sources, they often lack practical industry exposure and organizational familiarity, leading to early operational bottlenecks or coordination delays. However, through structural workplace orientation, technical training programs, and regular operational mentoring, these engineers quickly overcame their practical limitations, synchronized their collaborative actions, and mastered their professional responsibilities.<br><br>Conclusion: Therefore, systematic training successfully closed the gap between academic capability and corporate execution. It transformed the fresh graduates into highly coordinated, organization-specific assets, which directly enabled Megha Automobile Ltd. to overcome its initial delays and confidently achieve its long-term production and customer service goals."
