                        "label": "b",
                        "text": "Why is division of labor essential in an organization?",
                        "answer": "Enhancing Efficiency and Specialization: Division of labor breaks down a large, complex task into smaller, manageable parts and assigns them to employees based on their qualifications and skills. When an employee repeatedly performs the same specific task, they attain expertise and efficiency, which significantly reduces production costs and time wastage.<br><br>Ensuring Smooth Organizational Flow: Without proper division of labor, there arises a risk of duplication of work, internal conflicts, and role ambiguity. Therefore, to ensure maximum utilization of human resources, establish accountability, and maintain an orderly workflow, division of labor is essential in any organization."
