                        "text": "What is meant by the optimum span of supervision/control?",
                        "answer": "Definition of Span of Supervision: The span of supervision (or span of control) refers to the specific number of subordinates or workers that a single manager or superior can effectively direct, monitor, and control. It determines the horizontal scale and layers of management within an organizational hierarchy.<br><br>Significance of the \"Optimum\" Range: An optimum span means the number of subordinates is neither too large nor too small, but perfectly balanced according to the executive's capability and the nature of the work. If the span is optimum, it ensures effective supervision, minimizes communication delays, reduces operational expenses, and maximizes worker accountability and productivity."
