                "questions": [
                    {
                        "label": "a",
                        "text": "What is employee selection?",
                        "answer": "Employee selection is the process of evaluating and screening applicants to choose the most suitable and qualified candidates for vacant positions from the pool of recruited individuals."
                    },
                    {
                        "label": "b",
                        "text": "Why is staffing important in management? Explain.",
                        "answer": "Concept of Staffing:<br><br>Staffing is considered a vital function of management because human resources are the active driving force that transforms all passive, material resources into productive organizational outputs.<br><br>Explanation of Importance:<br><br>Without an efficient and well-placed workforce, even the most advanced machinery, financial capital, and detailed plans remain entirely ineffective. Systematic staffing ensures that the right person is assigned to the right job at the right time, directly reducing operational wastage, enhancing productivity, and boosting workplace morale. It serves as the continuous foundation for building, maintaining, and developing the organizational structure, making it indispensable for long-term institutional success."
                    },
                    {
                        "label": "c",
                        "text": "Which source of recruitment was used in the stem's organization? Explain.",
                        "answer": "Identification:<br><br>The organization in the stem used an External Source (specifically, advertisement in a newspaper) for recruiting its employees.<br><br>Theoretical Explanation:<br><br>The external source of recruitment refers to attracting and gathering potential job candidates from outside the organization's current workforce boundaries. Common methods of external recruitment include newspaper and online advertisements, job portals, educational institutions, employment exchanges, and professional agencies. This source allows an enterprise to access a vast, diverse, and competitive talent pool, injecting fresh perspective, new skills, and highly qualified professionals into the establishment.<br><br>Contextual Application:<br><br>In the stem, Aanmona Limited aimed to gather prospective candidates by publishing an explicit vacancy notice in a newspaper, detailing structural criteria such as required qualifications, experience, and age. Because the medium chosen was a public newspaper open to the open job market rather than an internal memo or reference, it drew an extensive response of 1,000 applications from outside applicants. Therefore, it is evident that the company relied completely on an external source of recruitment to meet its manpower needs."
                    },
                    {
                        "label": "d",
                        "text": "Identify the type of ongoing training method in the stem's organization and evaluate its rationale.",
                        "answer": "Identification:<br><br>The ongoing training method used in the organization is Job Rotation (পদ আবর্তন), which is an on-the-job training technique.<br><br>Theoretical Explanation:<br><br>Job rotation is a systematic management development method where an employee is deliberately shifted through a series of different positions, desks, or departments within the same organization. While the overall rank and salary remain unchanged, the job tasks vary significantly at each stage. This practical technique prevents workplace monotony, breaks routine boredom, and multi-skills the workforce, giving them a holistic understanding of how different organizational functions interconnect.<br><br>Contextual Application:<br><br>According to the stem, the management of Aanmona Limited did not confine the 40 newly appointed employees to a single isolated station. Instead, they structurally mandated that each worker spend one month in 6 different departments sequentially. By doing this, the trainees gain hands-on experience in production, marketing, quality control, and other core departments, directly exposing them to the full operational cycle of a manufacturing enterprise.<br><br>Analytical Evaluation:<br><br>The rationale behind this training approach is highly justified and strategically sound for a manufacturing enterprise like a rod factory. By rotating through multiple departments, the employees acquire versatile skill sets, making them highly flexible assets who can step in during labor shortages or operational crises. Furthermore, experiencing the diverse facets of the company removes insular thinking, fosters better inter-departmental coordination, and prepares these individuals for future cross-functional leadership roles, ultimately maximizing organizational productivity."
                    }
                ]
