                        "answer": "In the stem, Mr. Maruf initially followed an \"Autocratic Leadership\" (স্বৈরতান্ত্রিক নেতৃত্ব) style.<br><br>Autocratic leadership is a style where all decision-making authority is completely centralized in the hands of the leader, who imposes their own choices without taking any advice or feedback from subordinates. This management style neglects human relationships, treats employees like machines, and heavily induces job dissatisfaction, which ultimately reduces overall organizational performance and profitability.<br><br>According to the stem, Mr. Maruf did not seek or accept opinions from his subordinates for any work, carrying out tasks solely based on his personal wishes. This absolute centralized control caused widespread resentment among his workforce and directly dragged down the company's profitability. This behavior perfectly aligns with the characteristics of autocratic leadership."
