                        "text": "Direction always flows downward—Explain.",
                        "answer": "Direction always flows downward because instructions, orders, and guidance naturally originate from higher-level management and travel down the organizational hierarchy to lower-level executives or workers.<br><br>In a structured management system, top-level managers hold the primary decision-making power and strategic vision. They convert these goals into clear directives, operational plans, and rules, which are then passed down sequentially to middle and lower management for execution. Subordinates lack the authority to issue orders to their superiors, making direction a strictly downward, vertical flow of administrative communication."
