                        "answer": "An ideal leader must be patient because managing human resources involves handling diverse mindsets, sudden industrial changes, and operational crises that cannot be resolved through impulsive actions.<br><br>In a dynamic business environment, mistakes by subordinates, market disruptions, or strategic failures are common. A patient leader maintains composure, thoroughly analyzes the root causes of problems, and guides the team with stability, preventing workplace chaos and ensuring logical, long-term decision-making."
