                "stem": "Mr. Hosen consults with officers and employees of all levels before making decisions in his factory. This creates a positive perception among the workers toward the administration. As a result, production in the organization is continuously increasing. On the other hand, Mr. Kader does not take any employee's advice when making decisions in his factory. He makes decisions completely alone and forces everyone to implement them. This increases workers' dissatisfaction toward the administration, and production is continuously decreasing.",
