                        "answer": "Yes, the statement is highly justified and accurate; Mr. Kader’s \"Autocratic Leadership\" (স্বৈратান্ত্রিক নেতৃত্ব) style severely damages organizational stability in the long run, paralyzes human productivity, and can lead to permanent business failure.<br><br>Autocratic leadership is an authoritarian management style where the executive centralizes all decision-making power, acts completely in isolation, and relies entirely on force, tight surveillance, and fear to ensure absolute compliance. Subordinates are completely denied a voice in the corporate loop, which systematically destroys employee morale, creates deep operational resentment, and alienates talent from the company’s structural vision.<br><br>As displayed in the file image_e4d0cb.png, Mr. Kader completely ignores his employees' field insights, designs factory policies entirely by himself, and aggressively forces his workforce to execute those isolated commands. This rigid environment caused worker dissatisfaction toward the factory administration to escalate rapidly. Because the employees feel completely detached from the planning phase, their motivation collapsed, which triggered a continuous and critical decline in factory production metrics.<br><br>Therefore, it can be concluded that maintaining such a centralized, fear-based environment poses a fatal threat to the long-term survival of the enterprise. Persistent production drops, heavy resource wastage, and a highly disgruntled workforce inevitably lead to massive financial losses and operational paralysis. This proves that Mr. Kader's autocratic style is fundamentally toxic to the sustainable viability of the organization."
