                    {
                        "label": "d",
                        "text": "For which problem of leadership is the profit of the organization declining? Give your opinion.",
                        "answer": "The profit of the organization is declining due to a critical leadership and managerial flaw known as the \"Lack of Control and Accountability\" (নিয়ন্ত্রণের অভাব বা জবাবদিহিতার অনুপস্থিতি), which manifests here as a shift toward \"Laissez-faire / Free-rein Leadership\" (লাগামহীন বা মুক্ত নেতৃত্ব) traits in the execution phase.<br><br>In successful corporate governance, planning and setting targets represent only the first half of a leader's job; the second, equally vital half is controlling. Controlling is the systematic process of evaluating actual performance against pre-set standards, measuring deviations, and enforcing strict accountability. If a leader completely detaches themselves from checking the actual execution of work, an accountability vacuum is created. Without active supervision and tracking, worker discipline dissolves, resource wastage increases, and operational focus collapses.<br><br>As displayed in the file image_e4d888.png, while Mr. Rasel is excellent at consulting his team to set work goals, he completely fails to take any account, follow-up, or audit of the work actually performed by the workers. By failing to monitor performance, his leadership unconsciously degraded into a detached, laissez-faire behavior during the execution stage. Because the workers realized that no one was checking their final output, their productivity dropped continuously, causing corporate efficiency to fail and ultimately dragging down the organization's profits.<br><br>Therefore, it is my firm opinion that a plan without control is completely ineffective. To arrest the declining profits, Mr. Rasel must immediately resolve this oversight by establishing an unbroken supervisory framework. By pairing his democratic goal-setting with regular performance evaluations and accountability mechanisms, he can restore workplace vigilance, boost productivity, and return the enterprise to commercial growth."
                    }
