                        "answer": "Yes, I entirely agree with the statement. Mr. Bichitra Sen follows \"Laissez-faire or Free-rein Leadership\" (লাগামহীন বা মুক্ত নেতৃত্ব), which boosts individual creativity but severely weakens team cohesion.<br><br>Laissez-faire leadership is an open style where the leader completely detaches themselves from daily management, abdicates decision-making power, and gives full autonomy to subordinates. This approach is highly effective for fostering personal creativity because employees enjoy absolute professional freedom, allowing them to experiment with innovative solutions, think independently, and develop unique strategic designs without any fear of managerial intervention or overbearing supervision.<br><br>As displayed in the file image_e4eb8f.png, Mr. Bichitra Sen leaves his workers completely to themselves, allowing them to make all structural decisions independently. While this environment gives BSB Company's workforce the freedom to enhance their individual creative capacities, it naturally backfires when trying to preserve collective team unity. Because there is no active central authority to guide, mediate, or coordinate tasks, a severe management vacuum forms. Workers begin operating completely in isolation, which inevitably leads to severe internal conflicts, lack of alignment, and structural chaos within the firm.<br><br>Therefore, it can be firmly analyzed that while free-rein leadership acts as a catalyst for individual ingenuity, it is an ineffective method for maintaining team cohesion. Without a strong leader to harmonize individual goals, coordinate cross-functional efforts, and enforce shared accountability, the organizational parts fall apart. To maintain operational stability alongside creative growth, an enterprise must shift away from complete non-intervention and implement a balanced, consultative framework that preserves both team discipline and individual innovation."
