                        "answer": "\"Control is a continuous process\" means that control is not a one-time or final activity in management; rather, it is a cyclical, ongoing task that must be performed regularly alongside operational workflows.<br><br>As long as organizational activities exist, management must consistently establish performance standards, evaluate actual performance against those standards, identify deviations, and implement corrective measures. Once corrective actions are taken, new plans are formulated, and the controlling process starts anew, making it a never-ending cycle within the administrative framework."
