                        "text": "Why is it necessary to fulfill physiological needs? Explain.",
                        "answer": "Concept of Physiological Needs: Fulfilling physiological (or biological) needs is necessary because these are the basic, fundamental requirements for human survival and form the absolute base of human motivation.<br><br>Detailed Explanation: According to Abraham Maslow's theory, biological needs include primary essentials such as food, water, clothing, shelter, sleep, and air. If these fundamental survival needs remain unaddressed, a person cannot function physically or mentally, and higher-level desires (like safety or social status) will fail to arise. In an organizational context, ensuring the satisfaction of these biological needs through a fair basic wage is critical because a starving or physically exhausted worker cannot deliver productivity or stay dedicated to institutional goals."
