                "id": "15",
                "stem": "Look at the diagram below and answer questions C and D:<br><br><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 800 240\" width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\"> <defs> <marker id=\"arrow\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"6\" markerHeight=\"6\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"> <path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 6 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\" /> </marker> <style> .node-text { font-family: 'Arial', 'Helvetica', sans-serif; font-size: 16px; fill: #000000; text-anchor: middle; } .node-text-bold { font-weight: bold; font-size: 18px; } .flow-ellipse { stroke: #000000; stroke-width: 1.5; fill: #FFFFFF; } .flow-line { stroke: #000000; stroke-width: 1.5; fill: none; } </style> </defs> <rect width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" /> <ellipse cx=\"110\" cy=\"50\" rx=\"85\" ry=\"25\" class=\"flow-ellipse\" /> <text x=\"110\" y=\"55\" class=\"node-text\">Source of Information</text> <line x1=\"195\" y1=\"50\" x2=\"225\" y2=\"50\" class=\"flow-line\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow)\" /> <ellipse cx=\"305\" cy=\"50\" rx=\"75\" ry=\"25\" class=\"flow-ellipse\" /> <text x=\"305\" y=\"55\" class=\"node-text\">Sender</text> <line x1=\"380\" y1=\"50\" x2=\"410\" y2=\"50\" class=\"flow-line\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow)\" /> <ellipse cx=\"490\" cy=\"50\" rx=\"75\" ry=\"25\" class=\"flow-ellipse\" /> <text x=\"490\" y=\"55\" class=\"node-text\">Encoding</text> <line x1=\"565\" y1=\"50\" x2=\"595\" y2=\"50\" class=\"flow-line\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow)\" /> <ellipse cx=\"675\" cy=\"50\" rx=\"75\" ry=\"25\" class=\"flow-ellipse\" /> <text x=\"675\" y=\"55\" class=\"node-text\">Message / Info</text> <line x1=\"675\" y1=\"75\" x2=\"675\" y2=\"95\" class=\"flow-line\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow)\" /> <ellipse cx=\"675\" cy=\"122\" rx=\"75\" ry=\"25\" class=\"flow-ellipse\" /> <text x=\"675\" y=\"127\" class=\"node-text\">Medium</text> <line x1=\"675\" y1=\"147\" x2=\"675\" y2=\"167\" class=\"flow-line\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow)\" /> <ellipse cx=\"675\" cy=\"195\" rx=\"75\" ry=\"25\" class=\"flow-ellipse\" /> <text x=\"675\" y=\"200\" class=\"node-text\">Receiver</text> <line x1=\"600\" y1=\"195\" x2=\"570\" y2=\"195\" class=\"flow-line\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow)\" /> <ellipse cx=\"490\" cy=\"195\" rx=\"75\" ry=\"25\" class=\"flow-ellipse\" /> <text x=\"490\" y=\"200\" class=\"node-text\">Decoding</text> <line x1=\"415\" y1=\"195\" x2=\"385\" y2=\"195\" class=\"flow-line\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow)\" /> <ellipse cx=\"305\" cy=\"195\" rx=\"75\" ry=\"25\" class=\"flow-ellipse\" /> <text x=\"305\" y=\"201\" class=\"node-text node-text-bold\">A</text> <line x1=\"305\" y1=\"170\" x2=\"305\" y2=\"82\" class=\"flow-line\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow)\" /> </svg>",
                "meta": "Rajshahi Board · 2017",
                "type": "board",
                "questions": [
                    {
                        "label": "a",
                        "text": "What is E-mail?",
                        "answer": "E-mail (Electronic Mail) is a digital method of exchanging messages or data from one computer or digital device to another over the internet."
                    },
                    {
                        "label": "b",
                        "text": "What is meant by video conferencing?",
                        "answer": "Video conferencing is a modern telecommunication technology that allows two or more people in different geographical locations to interact via two-way video and audio transmissions in real-time. It creates a virtual face-to-face meeting environment without requiring physical travel.<br><br>Through this system, participants can not only hear each other but also see expressions, share documents, and collaborate on presentations instantly. It is widely used in modern business management for holding virtual meetings, training sessions, and interviews, which significantly saves time and reduces operational costs."
                    },
                    {
                        "label": "c",
                        "text": "Which process in management is indicated by the given diagram? Explain.",
                        "answer": "The diagram given in the stem indicates the Communication Process (যোগাযোগ প্রক্রিয়া) in management.<br><br>Communication is the exchange of facts, ideas, opinions, or emotions between two or more persons to create a mutual understanding. In management, the communication process represents a continuous loop where information flows systematically from a sender to a receiver and concludes with the receiver's response or feedback. The diagram sequentially illustrates all the essential components—starting from the source of information to encoding, transmission via a medium, decoding, and ending with feedback—which perfectly represents a complete communication cycle.<br><br>In this illustrated process, the sender first originates an idea (Information Source) and converts it into a transmittable form (Encoding). This encoded 'Message' is then sent through a specific 'Medium' to the 'Receiver'. Upon receiving the message, the receiver interprets its meaning (Decoding) and sends a response back to the sender, completing the managerial communication cycle necessary for organizational coordination and decision-making."
                    },
                    {
                        "label": "d",
                        "text": "Evaluate the role of the element marked 'A' in the given process.",
                        "answer": "In the given communication process diagram, the element marked 'A' represents Feedback (প্রতিপুষ্টি), which plays a critical role in making the communication effective and complete.<br><br>Feedback is the receiver's response to the sender's message, indicating how the message was interpreted. Without feedback, communication remains a one-way process, leaving the sender uncertain whether the message was received, understood correctly, or misinterpreted. In the provided chart, the arrow from 'A' points directly back to the 'Sender', which confirms that 'A' is the concluding step that closes the communication loop.<br><br>The vital roles of feedback ('A') in this process are evaluated through the following key points:<br><br>* Ensuring Complete Communication: Communication is incomplete without a response. Feedback transforms one-way information transmission into a meaningful two-way interactive process.<br><br>* Measuring Accuracy and Understanding: It allows the sender to verify whether the receiver has understood the core message exactly as intended, minimizing the risks of misunderstandings or errors.<br><br>* Basis for Future Action: In management, feedback serves as a continuous evaluation tool, enabling managers to adjust their strategies, resolve conflicts, and make informed decisions based on the subordinate's reactions or reports.<br><br>In conclusion, feedback ('A') acts as the backbone of successful organizational communication. Without it, the entire communication cycle shown in the diagram would break down, rendering managerial directives ineffective and leaving the organization vulnerable to miscoordination."
                    }
                ]
