                        "answer": "The communication process refers to the systematic step-by-step sequence through which a message originates from a sender and travels via a medium to a receiver, who then decodes it and provides feedback to complete the loop.<br><br>This process involves a series of interrelated elements: developing an idea, encoding, selecting a transmission channel, receiving, decoding, and interpreting. In management, understanding this continuous cycle is essential because any breakdown or noise in these sequential steps will lead to a failure in delivering the exact corporate directive."
