                        "label": "b",
                        "text": "Explain the communication process. (With diagram)",
                        "answer": "The communication process refers to the systematic step-by-step sequence through which a message originates from a sender, gets converted into symbols, travels through a specific channel to a receiver, and concludes with a return response.<br><br>This continuous cycle forms the framework of organizational interaction, ensuring information flows without distortion.<br><br>The sequential steps involved in this operational process are as follows:<br><br>* Developing an Idea: The sender first conceives a thought, fact, or objective that needs to be shared.<br><br>* Encoding: The conceived idea is converted into words, symbols, gestures, or written scripts for transmission.<br><br>* Selecting a Medium: A suitable transmission channel (e.g., e-mail, telephone, letter) is chosen.<br><br>* Transmitting the Message: The encoded message is physically or electronically sent through the selected channel.<br><br>* Receiving: The designated receiver collects the transmitted signal.<br><br>* Decoding: The receiver translates and interprets the encoded symbols into understandable meaning.<br><br>* Feedback: The receiver transmits a response back to the sender, confirming accurate understanding and completing the loop."
