                        "answer": "The statement \"The role of information and communication technology in the development of business and commerce is undeniable\" is completely accurate and supported by modern corporate dynamics.<br><br>Information and Communication Technology (ICT) serves as the digital engine of modern commerce, systematically transforming traditional paper-bound administration into a highly responsive, high-speed ecosystem. By integrating internet-enabled networks and software solutions, enterprises can eliminate geographic boundaries, maximize data processing speed, and drastically reduce operational friction.<br><br>The undeniable impacts of ICT on Rupsha Bank's management are analyzed through the following points:<br><br>* Instantaneous Top-Down Directives: Mr. Noman utilizes corporate e-mail networks to simultaneously broadcast monthly operational targets to all scattered branch managers the moment he arrives at the office, eliminating logistical lag.<br><br>* Rapid and Structured Bottom-Up Reporting: The branch managers compile and transmit their strategic work plans back to the Managing Director via e-mail instantly, facilitating highly agile corporate monitoring and swift strategic alignment.<br><br>* Substantial Reduction in Overhead Costs: Shifting the vast majority of regular inter-branch correspondence from physical paper mail to electronic communication slashes the firm's administrative, printing, and transit expenditures.<br><br>* Enhanced Accuracy and Data Preservation: Utilizing a digital medium automatically logs every email and attachment, building an unalterable text record that streamlines compliance audits and ensures long-term operational transparency.<br><br>In conclusion, the widespread use of electronic mail between the top executive and branch heads at Rupsha Bank clearly demonstrates how digital tools accelerate internal processes. ICT injects unparalleled speed, structural precision, and cost-efficiency into daily corporate workflows, making its role absolutely vital for the development and competitive survival of any modern business."
