                        "text": "What is meant by the Break-Even Point (BEP)? Explain.",
                        "answer": "Knowledge: The Break-Even Point (BEP) is the specific volume of sales or production at which an enterprise's total revenue exactly equals its total costs, resulting in neither profit nor loss.<br><br>Realization: In business management, BEP serves as a vital financial control tool. Below this point, the company operates at a loss because it cannot cover its fixed overhead expenses. Above this point, the firm begins to generate a net profit. Calculating the BEP helps managers determine minimum sales targets, set safe product pricing strategies, and control operational costs to ensure the business remains financially viable."
