                        "answer": "Knowledge (Para 1): The Break-Even Point (BEP) in units for \"Good Food\" company is 1,000 units, and the Break-Even Point in value is 2,000,000 Tk.<br><br>Mathematical Calculation (Para 2): To find the BEP, we must first categorize the data into Total Fixed Costs (FC) and Variable Cost per Unit (VC):<br><br>• Selling Price per Unit ($P$) = 2,000 Tk.<br><br>1. Variable Cost per Unit ($VC$):<br><br>• Raw Material Cost per Unit = 1,000 Tk.<br><br>• Wage per Unit = 200 Tk.<br><br>• Total Variable Cost per Unit ($VC$) = $1,000 + 200 = 1,200 \\text{ Tk.}$<br><br>2. Total Fixed Costs ($FC$):<br><br>• Building Rent = 250,000 Tk.<br><br>• Officers' Salaries = 500,000 Tk.<br><br>• Annual Electricity Bill = 50,000 Tk.<br><br>• Total Fixed Costs ($FC$) = $250,000 + 500,000 + 50,000 = 800,000 \\text{ Tk.}$<br><br>3. Break-Even Point (BEP) Formula and Calculation:<br><br>$$\\text{BEP (in units)} = \\frac{\\text{Total Fixed Costs (FC)}}{\\text{Selling Price per Unit (P)} - \\text{Variable Cost per Unit (VC)}}$$<br><br>$$\\text{BEP (in units)} = \\frac{800,000}{2,000 - 1,200} = \\frac{800,000}{800} = 1,000 \\text{ units}$$<br><br>$$\\text{BEP (in sales value)} = 1,000 \\text{ units} \\times 2,000 \\text{ Tk./unit} = 2,000,000 \\text{ Tk.}$$<br><br>Explanation & Conclusion (Para 3): In management control, the break-even point serves as a critical quantitative baseline. The calculation proves that \"Good Food\" company must manufacture and sell exactly 1,000 units of its product (generating 2,000,000 Tk. in revenue) to reach a state of zero profit and zero loss. Selling anything below this threshold will result in structural financial losses for the factory."
