                                        "text": "What is meant by a statutory body?",
                                        "answer": "Paragraph 1: Definition of Statutory Body<br><br>A statutory body (or statutory public corporation) is an autonomous corporate entity established through a special act passed in the national parliament or by a specific decree/order issued by the head of state.<br><br>Paragraph 2: Operational Features<br><br>These organizations are entirely owned and financed by the state, with public welfare as their primary operational motive. Unlike traditional government departments, a statutory body enjoys artificial legal personality, continuous succession, and operational independence. This enables it to carry out daily commercial or administrative activities efficiently without being constrained by rigid bureaucratic red tape."
