                                        "answer": "Paragraph 1: Cognitive Identification<br><br>Based on ownership, 'Shoukhin Motel' is a state-owned enterprise, specifically running under a statutory public corporation (Bangladesh Parjatan Corporation).<br><br>Paragraph 2: Conceptual Explanation<br><br>State-owned enterprises are business organizations established, owned, funded, and managed by the central government or state authorities to ensure public welfare and strategic national development. When such an entity is created via a special legislative act or a presidential decree, it receives corporate autonomy, allowing its management to run the business professionally while the state retains ultimate control over policy, capital, and assets.<br><br>Paragraph 3: Contextual Application<br><br>The stem highlights that 'Shoukhin Motel' operates under an organization formed in 1972 by a presidential decree. In Bangladesh, the hospitality and tourism sector's public assets are managed by the Bangladesh Parjatan Corporation, which was established by Presidential Order No. 143 in 1972. Because this overarching organization is state-owned and statutory, any sub-unit or motel it runs automatically falls under the classification of state-owned service organizations. Therefore, Shoukhin Motel is a state-owned business structure."
