                                        "answer": "Paragraph 1: Definition of BSCIC<br><br>BSCIC stands for Bangladesh Small and Cottage Industries Corporation, which is a statutory public corporation established by the government to promote, support, and accelerate the development of small, cottage, and medium-scale industries across the country.<br><br>Paragraph 2: Core Functions and Significance<br><br>BSCIC plays a crucial role in industrialization by creating industrial estates (BSCIC industrial zones), providing infrastructural facilities, giving technical and managerial training to new entrepreneurs, and offering advisory services. By assisting grassroots businesses with raw material sourcing and credit facilities, it aims to reduce poverty, generate regional employment, and boost the national economy through balanced decentralized growth."
