                                        "answer": "The institution mentioned in the stem is a Statutory Corporation (রাষ্ট্রীয় বিধিবদ্ধ সংস্থা). A statutory corporation is an autonomous entity created by a specific law passed in the national parliament to carry out specialized public services, such as transportation or utility supply.<br><br>These institutions are characterized by their own legal personality and a separate administrative structure. The government provides the initial capital, and the institution is run by a board of directors appointed by the government, operating independently while remaining accountable to the legislature.<br><br>Since the stem mentions that the government passed a law in parliament specifically to establish this transportation institution, it fits the definition and legal framework of a statutory corporation perfectly."
