                                        "answer": "The PPP model described in the stem is the \"Build-Operate-Transfer\" (BOT) model.<br><br>In a BOT contract, the private party (in this case, the foreign company) is responsible for the design, construction, and operation of a project for a specified period (10 years here). During this time, they manage the facility and often derive revenue from it to recover their investment and operational costs. After the expiration of the concession period, the ownership and management responsibility are transferred back to the public authority (the government).<br><br>This model is particularly useful for governments that lack the necessary technical expertise or technology but have the capital, allowing them to benefit from private sector efficiency for a duration before assuming full control."
