                                        "answer": "To address the infringement by \"Y\" publication house, the following legal actions are recommended:<br><br>1. Issuing a Legal Notice: The primary step is to issue a formal legal notice to \"Y\" publication house, demanding them to immediately stop the publication and distribution of the pirated book and to withdraw all copies from the market.<br><br>2. Seeking an Injunction (Stay Order): \"X\" publication should move the court to obtain an immediate injunction. This will legally force \"Y\" to stop all sales and production of the infringing book until the final judgment is passed, preventing further financial loss.<br><br>3. Filing for Damages and Compensation: \"X\" publication house should file a civil lawsuit claiming damages for the loss of sales and reputation caused by the infringement. The court can order \"Y\" to compensate \"X\" for the profits lost due to their illegal activity.<br><br>4. Criminal Prosecution for Infringement: Under the Copyright Act, copyright infringement is also a criminal offense. \"X\" can initiate criminal proceedings, which may lead to the seizure of the illegal copies, imprisonment, or hefty fines for the owners of \"Y\" publication, ensuring a strong deterrent effect."
