                                                                "text": "What is meant by an intense desire for achievement? Explain.",
                                                                "answer": "An intense desire for achievement (কৃতিত্ব অর্জনের তীব্র আকাঙ্ক্ষা) refers to an individual's strong psychological drive and internal motivation to excel, overcome complex obstacles, master difficult challenges, and attain significant personal or professional success. It is a core behavioral trait that pushes a person to set high standards of performance and find satisfaction in successfully executing difficult tasks through their own capabilities.<br><br>In entrepreneurial psychology, this drive is more powerful than the mere desire for financial profit. It gives a business leader the mental resilience needed to endure initial business losses, ignore social skepticism, and continuously optimize production processes, ensuring long-term operational sustainability in a competitive market ecosystem."
