                                                                "label": "b",
                                                                "text": "Describe the bad effects of the production and use of polythene.",
                                                                "answer": "The production and use of polythene have devastating, long-term bad effects on the ecosystem because it is a non-biodegradable synthetic polymer that takes hundreds of years to decompose.<br><br>When carelessly discarded, polythene bags clog urban sewage and drainage systems, leading to artificial waterlogging and stagnant, toxic water. Furthermore, when mixed with agricultural topsoil, it forms an impermeable layer that blocks the natural flow of water, air, and organic nutrients, which suffocates plant roots and permanently degrades soil fertility. If burned, it releases highly carcinogenic gases into the air, triggering severe respiratory illnesses and atmospheric degradation."
